---
import PolicyPage from "../components/PolicyPage.astro";
---

<PolicyPage
  title="Terms & Conditions"
  description="Read the terms for shopping handmade chocolates from Chocolate Circle."
  kicker="The important bits"
>
  <p>
    These draft terms apply to orders placed through Chocolate Circle. Before publishing, replace
    all bracketed prompts and make sure the terms reflect how the shop actually operates.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    This shop is operated by <strong>[ADD FULL LEGAL BUSINESS OR OWNER NAME]</strong>, trading as
    Chocolate Circle, at <strong>[ADD REGISTERED BUSINESS ADDRESS]</strong>. Business or food
    registration details, where applicable: <strong>[ADD REQUIRED REGISTRATION DETAILS]</strong>.
    Contact: <strong>[ADD CUSTOMER SUPPORT EMAIL AND PHONE]</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Products, ingredients, and availability</h2>
  <p>
    We make handmade chocolate in small batches. Product descriptions, photographs, prices,
    weights, ingredients, and allergen information must be checked on the relevant product and
    its packaging. Replace sample catalogue content and add verified ingredient and allergen
    information before selling. Contact us before ordering if you have an allergy or dietary
    question; do not rely on an unverified website description.
  </p>
  <p>
    Products are subject to availability. If we cannot fulfil a paid order, we will contact you
    using the details you provide and explain the options available under our published
    cancellation and refund policy.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Prices, orders, and payment</h2>
  <p>
    Product prices are shown in Indian rupees. The checkout currently calculates the chocolate
    subtotal only; it does not calculate or add a delivery charge. Do not accept live payments
    until any delivery charge is displayed in the checkout total before the customer pays.
    Payment is processed by Razorpay under its applicable terms. A payment confirmation does not
    replace any required delivery-area or product-availability confirmation.
  </p>
  <p>
    The customer is responsible for providing a correct name, phone number, email address if
    supplied, and delivery address. We use these details to process and fulfil the order, as
    described in our <a href="../privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Delivery</h2>
  <p>
    We use the delivery pin you provide to estimate the straight-line distance from the shop.
    Orders at or within 15 km are marked for manual Porter booking; orders beyond 15 km are
    marked for a manually arranged courier. These are suggestions for the shop only; no carrier
    is automatically booked, and the shop must confirm that the address, delivery option, and
    any fee work before fulfilment. Straight-line distance is not road distance. See our
    <a href="../shipping-policy/">Shipping Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Changes, cancellations, and refunds</h2>
  <p>
    Add the shop's actual cancellation cut-off, how customers request a change or cancellation,
    how damaged, incorrect, missing, or delayed orders are reported, evidence and reporting
    timeframes if applicable, and the available refund or replacement process:
    <strong>[ADD A COMPLETE CANCELLATION, RETURNS, AND REFUND POLICY REVIEWED FOR APPLICABLE LAW]</strong>.
    Do not publish this draft or take live orders until this section is complete. Nothing in
    these terms limits any customer rights that cannot legally be excluded.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Our <a href="../privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains what information is collected
    during checkout, how it is shared with checkout providers, and how to contact us about it.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Issues and applicable law</h2>
  <p>
    Questions or complaints: <strong>[ADD CUSTOMER SUPPORT EMAIL AND PHONE]</strong>. Add
    applicable governing law, dispute-resolution steps, and jurisdiction after legal review:
    <strong>[ADD APPLICABLE LEGAL AND DISPUTE DETAILS]</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    If these terms change, update the effective date and make the current version available
    before customers place an order.
  </p>
</PolicyPage>
